@startuml
title GET /api/v1/games
hide footbox
actor Client
participant "FastAPI / Pydantic" as API
participant "SQLAlchemy session" as DB
database PostgreSQL as PG
Client -> API: GET /api/v1/games
API -> API: Validate path, query and body
note over API: Invalid input -> 422
No authentication required
API -> DB: get_db(): request transaction
DB -> PG: Select games; combine optional pod_id and result-existence filters
DB -> PG: Order by game_id; apply limit/offset
DB -> PG: Eager-load players and results for selected games
PG --> DB: Rows / mutation outcome
DB --> API: Route result
API -> API: Validate/serialize response
API -> DB: Finish successful request
DB -> PG: COMMIT
API --> Client: 200
note over API, PG: Any failure aborts the success path and rolls back.
See transaction.puml for shared error handling.
@enduml
